00:00:00.150 --> 00:00:04.249 line:2 align:center
Let's follow the token
cold. Its query vector,

2
00:00:04.249 --> 00:00:10.950 line:2 align:center
in red, is compared with the key vector
of every token in the sentence, in green.

3
00:00:11.150 --> 00:00:15.179 line:2 align:center
Each score is the query
for cold dotted with a key,

4
00:00:15.179 --> 00:00:20.991 line:2 align:center
then divided by the square root of
d. The scaled scores are minus 0.5,

5
00:00:20.991 --> 00:00:27.150 line:2 align:center
0.2, 1.3, 0.6, and 1.6.

6
00:00:27.350 --> 00:00:31.854 line:2 align:center
The highest scores go to cold
itself, at 1.6, and to has,

7
00:00:31.854 --> 00:00:37.483 line:2 align:center
at 1.3. These are the tokens
that matter most here.

8
00:00:37.683 --> 00:00:41.485 line:2 align:center
A softmax turns the five
scores into attention weights.

9
00:00:41.485 --> 00:00:46.883 line:2 align:center
They are all between zero and
one, and together they sum to one.

10
00:00:47.083 --> 00:00:52.264 line:2 align:center
The new vector for cold is the
weighted sum of the five value vectors,

11
00:00:52.264 --> 00:00:57.871 line:2 align:center
in blue. The values of has
and cold contribute the most.

12
00:01:00.083 --> 00:01:04.692 line:2 align:center
Now the vector for cold carries its
context. In the phrase has a cold,

13
00:01:04.692 --> 00:01:09.480 line:2 align:center
